-- plan.lth: the plan as a value: the dataflow of a cone, a schedule that linearizes it, the live
-- subgraph a demand reaches, the strategy as a parameter, the law `Confluent`, and the key under
-- which a result is kept.
--
-- Draft 0, 2026-10-15, by Claude Fable 5.1, an agent of the coordinating session, on the brief
-- record/IA/demand-2026-10-15/prompt.md (step 6.1 of
-- record/plan/luthier-from-zero/plan-from-zero-2026-10-13-execution.md). Sources: spec 8.S3,
-- 8.S4, 8.S5, 8.S8, 8.S9, 8.S10, 8.S11 (docs/spec/08-demand.md); L5.2, L5.6, L5.11, L5.13, L5.14,
-- P11; D-2026-10-10-d (forward on demand; results kept under a hash), D-2026-10-13-g (the plan a
-- value of this file, `Confluent` the law an order of evaluation is certified against; the key of
-- 8.S8), D-2026-10-14-c (every law Boolean); the retired `lib/plan.lut` at v0.1-final (a718abc:
-- `Dataflow`, `Schedule`, `Linearizes`, `run`, `Equivalent`, `Confluent` over `Fin n`), rewritten
-- over names; demand.lth (`Demand`); certification.lth §4 (the pattern of a hash's laws). Pattern
-- of certification.lth.
-- 2026-10-15, by Claude Opus 5.5, an agent of the coordinating session, on record/IA/
-- layer-3-review-2026-10-15/prompt-fix-BCD.md (item 2 of its summary-BCD.md, B7 to B9): a schedule
-- places every name after what it reads among the names it holds; `Dataflow` a theory, its names
-- unique, acyclic, its step reading only what its node lists (D-2026-10-10-c: what is forbidden is
-- what the graph does not show), with the equality of its values a parameter (4.R8); the roles of
-- the two strategies as laws of `Planning` (L2.7).
-- 2026-10-16, by Claude Opus 5.5, an agent of the coordinating session, on record/IA/
-- code-follows-2026-10-16/prompt-store.md (v0.4's criterion c; D-2026-10-15-d, D-2026-10-15-h): the
-- key of a run as a function of its record, its seed, its plan and the certificates (`keyOf`), the
-- law that run.py's key is that function (`KeyIsOfTheRecord`), and `determined` over the key's
-- hash (`ResultsDetermined`), the store of results run.py writes in `x.results.json`.
-- 2026-10-23, by Claude Sonnet 5.5, on record/plan/audit-algebras-2026-10-22/execution.md (A7; audit
-- 3.3, 3.4): the hash laws no longer say injectivity (a finite digest cannot be injective on an
-- unbounded space): the digest laws are collision evidence on listed cases, the lookup compares the
-- full key (`LookupComparesTheFullKey`) and never serves a cone with an action
-- (`ActionConeIsNeverServed`), and the determinacy of a pure cone under any strategy is a law
-- conditional on L4.7 (`PureConeIsDeterminate`). The semantic quotient (audit 3.5) is question 5 and waits.
--
-- What this file states. A dataflow says, for each name of a cone, what it reads and how its
-- value follows from theirs (8.S4: a demand's plan is the dataflow of its cone). A schedule is an
-- order of names; it linearizes the dataflow when it holds each live name once and none before
-- what it reads (L5.2: each node once and whole). Running a schedule computes the names in its
-- order; `Confluent` says any two linearizations give every name the same value, which holds
-- because a definition has no effects (8.S5), and is here a Boolean law a dataflow is certified
-- against (8.S11, L5.11), with the two schedules as the parameters a test draws. A plan is the
-- live subgraph the entry reaches with a schedule of it and the strategy that chose the order
-- (8.S4: the strategy is a parameter). The key of 8.S8 is stated with the laws a hash of it owes;
-- its model is run.py's (`result_key`, `key_hash`), so plan_model.lut gives it none. The
-- backward pass from a demand and a program to a dataflow is a hole (8.S11: not written). What
-- the brief or the spec leaves open is marked [proposed] at the item above it.
--
-- Index (all sections written in this draft):
--   §1 The dataflow over names; the live subgraph an entry reaches (8.S3, 8.S4, L5.13).     done
--   §2 Schedules: linearizing, running, `Confluent` (8.S5, 8.S11, L5.2, L5.11).             done
--   §3 The plan and the strategy; the backward pass as a hole (8.S4, 8.S11).                done
--   §4 The key of a result (8.S8, 8.S9, 8.S10, L5.6).                                       done
--   §5 The theory `Planning`, the laws of §2 to §4 claimed.                                  done

import "demand.lth" Demand Decoration RunRecord Stored determined Strategy ForwardOnDemand CallByNeed
import "certification.lth" Value Hash
import "generators.lth" Seed
import "term.lth" Term Program

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- §1 The dataflow

-- A node of the dataflow: a name and the names it reads (8.S6: a dependence is an edge; a
-- parameter is a node with nothing read). A dataflow over values of `A`: its nodes, the value a
-- name holds before it is computed, and how a name's value follows from the values so far.
-- [proposed] The nodes are listed in the program's order; a name read that no node defines is a
-- leaf that keeps `init` (a hole the demand did not fill is an error that flows, 8.S3).
-- [proposed] A dataflow is a theory over the values `A` and their equality `eq` (4.R8: `A` may
-- hold functions, so the law that compares values takes the equality): its laws state the role
-- of `reads` and of `step` (L2.7). Each name is defined by one node; no name reads itself through
-- any chain of reads (a program is a DAG, L9; a cycle has no schedule); and the value of a name
-- follows from the values of the names its node lists and of no other (D-2026-10-10-c, 8.S5: a
-- definition has no effects), which is what makes any two schedules agree (`Confluent`, §2).
-- Certified per dataflow (7.R4): a record of functions has no generator.
Node = { name : String, reads : List String }
Dataflow (A : U) (eq : A -> A -> Bool) : { nodes : List Node, init : A, step : String -> (String -> A) -> A }

subset (xs ys : List String) : Bool := all List String (fn (x : String) { member List String x ys }) xs
sameMembers (xs ys : List String) : Bool := subset xs ys and subset ys xs
names (ns : List Node) : List String := map Node String (fn (n : Node) { n.name }) ns
readsOf (ns : List Node) (x : String) : List String :=
  concat String (map Node (List String) (fn (n : Node) { n.reads }) (take Node 1 (filter List Node (fn (n : Node) { n.name == x }) ns)))
-- the names added at the end, each once, in the order met
addNew (xs new : List String) : List String :=
  foldLeft String (List String) (fn (acc : List String) (n : String) { if member List String n acc then acc else acc <> [n] }) xs new
readsOfAll (ns : List Node) (xs : List String) : List String :=
  fold String (List String) (fn a b { addNew a b }) nil (fn x { readsOf ns x }) xs
-- an environment that agrees with `env` on the names listed and with `other` elsewhere
agreeOn (A : U) (xs : List String) (env other : String -> A) : String -> A := fn m { if member List String m xs then env m else other m }
-- the names a name reaches by one read or more, closed in as many rounds as there are nodes
beyond (ns : List Node) (x : String) : List String := expand ns (readsOf ns x) (size ns)

NamesAreUnique (A : U) (eq : A -> A -> Bool) (d : Dataflow A eq) : Bool := distinct String (structural String) (names d.nodes)
Acyclic (A : U) (eq : A -> A -> Bool) (d : Dataflow A eq) : Bool :=
  all List String (fn (x : String) { not (member List String x (beyond d.nodes x)) }) (names d.nodes)
-- the step of a name gives one value on a drawn environment and on the same environment with every
-- name its node does not list back at `init`, the value of what is not computed: a step that reads
-- a name its node does not list is refuted where the environment holds something else there
StepIsLocal (A : U) (eq : A -> A -> Bool) (d : Dataflow A eq) (n : String) (env : String -> A) : Bool :=
  eq (d.step n env) (d.step n (agreeOn A (readsOf d.nodes n) env (fn m { d.init })))
Dataflow (A : U) (eq : A -> A -> Bool) := NamesAreUnique A eq & Acyclic A eq & StepIsLocal A eq

-- The live subgraph (8.S3, L5.13): what the entry reaches along `reads`, the backward pass over
-- names that computes no value; closed in as many rounds as there are nodes, so it ends on a
-- cycle too. What it does not reach, the complement of the cone, is not produced.
expand (ns : List Node) (seen : List String) (k : Nat) : List String :=
  if k == 0 then seen else expand ns (addNew seen (readsOfAll ns seen)) (k - 1)
reaches (A : U) (eq : A -> A -> Bool) (d : Dataflow A eq) (entry : String) : List String := expand d.nodes [entry] (size d.nodes)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- §2 Schedules

-- A schedule: names in the order they are computed. It linearizes a dataflow on a set of names
-- when it holds exactly those, each once (L5.2: each node once), and none before what it reads
-- among them (a name read outside the set is a leaf, §1): each name's reads that are in the set
-- are already placed when it is. [proposed] v0.1's check, rewritten over names, compared the reads
-- with the names already placed, which holds by construction, and accepted a read placed later:
-- `["d","b","c","a"]` linearized `example` and gave d = 0 (summary-BCD.md, item 2).
Schedule = List String
-- kept as a recursion (bite 13b): the placed names grow along the schedule (state threaded left to right)
placedBefore (ns : List Node) (live placed s : List String) : Bool :=
  match s { nil -> true ; cons n rest -> subset (keep live (readsOf ns n)) placed and placedBefore ns live (cons n placed) rest }
keep (within xs : List String) : List String := filter List String (fn x { member List String x within }) xs
LinearizesOn (A : U) (eq : A -> A -> Bool) (d : Dataflow A eq) (live : List String) (s : Schedule) : Bool :=
  sameMembers s live and distinct String (structural String) s and placedBefore d.nodes live nil s

-- Running a schedule: each name in its order, from the values so far; a name not scheduled keeps
-- `init`.
update (A : U) (env : String -> A) (n : String) (v : A) : String -> A := fn m { if m == n then v else env m }
runFrom (A : U) (eq : A -> A -> Bool) (d : Dataflow A eq) (s : Schedule) (env : String -> A) : String -> A :=
  foldLeft String (String -> A) (fn (e : String -> A) (n : String) { update A e n (d.step n e) }) env s
run (A : U) (eq : A -> A -> Bool) (d : Dataflow A eq) (s : Schedule) : String -> A := runFrom A eq d s (fn m { d.init })

-- Two schedules are equivalent on a set of names when every name of it gets the same value under
-- both; `Confluent` (8.S5, 8.S11, L5.11, D-2026-10-13-g): any two linearizations are equivalent.
-- The law a dataflow is certified against, with the schedules drawn; a session block reordered
-- is one more pair it covers (8.S14).
EquivalentOn (A : U) (eq : A -> A -> Bool) (d : Dataflow A eq) (live : List String) (s1 s2 : Schedule) : Bool :=
  all List String (fn (n : String) { eq (run A eq d s1 n) (run A eq d s2 n) }) live
Confluent (A : U) (eq : A -> A -> Bool) (d : Dataflow A eq) (live : List String) (s1 s2 : Schedule) : Bool :=
  not (LinearizesOn A eq d live s1 and LinearizesOn A eq d live s2) or EquivalentOn A eq d live s1 s2

-- [proposed, B11 of summary-BCD.md] A linearization built from drawn choices: at each step the
-- names of the set not yet placed whose reads among the set are placed are ready, and the choice
-- picks one of them (its index modulo how many are ready; the first when the choices run out).
-- Every linearization of an acyclic dataflow is one of these, and drawn schedules almost never
-- linearize, so the law over the plan compares with these and not with schedules drawn whole.
readyIn (ns : List Node) (live placed cands : List String) : List String :=
  filter List String (fn n { not (member List String n placed) and subset (keep live (readsOf ns n)) placed }) cands
atIndex (xs : List String) (i : Nat) : List String := match nth String xs i { just x -> [x] ; nothing -> nil }
headOr (cs : List Nat) : Nat := match nth Nat cs 0 { just c -> c ; nothing -> 0 }
tailOf (cs : List Nat) : List Nat := drop Nat 1 cs
readyOrder (ns : List Node) (live placed : List String) (cs : List Nat) (k : Nat) : Schedule :=
  if k == 0 then nil
  else match atIndex (readyIn ns live placed live) (headOr cs mod (1 + size (readyIn ns live placed live))) {
    nil -> (match readyIn ns live placed live { nil -> nil ; cons x rest -> cons x (readyOrder ns live (cons x placed) (tailOf cs) (k - 1)) }) ;
    cons x rest -> cons x (readyOrder ns live (cons x placed) (tailOf cs) (k - 1)) }
linearization (A : U) (eq : A -> A -> Bool) (d : Dataflow A eq) (live : List String) (cs : List Nat) : Schedule :=
  readyOrder d.nodes live nil cs (size live)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- §3 The plan

-- The strategy, a parameter separate from the program (8.S4, L5.2, P11): forward on demand, the
-- default 8.S3 decides (the live subgraph in topological order, computed strictly); or call by
-- need, what `run.py` does today (each name reduced at its first demand and kept), which computes
-- the same live subgraph in the order of first demand. Both are linearizations, so by `Confluent`
-- they agree. The strategy is a field of the demand (D-2026-10-16-d), so `Strategy` is declared
-- in demand.lth and imported here. What each constructor means is an order, stated as a law of
-- `Planning` (§5, L2.7): forward on demand places the names level by level, a name's level one
-- more than the highest level of what it reads among the live names; call by need places them in
-- the order of first demand, a depth-first visit from the entry in the order the reads are
-- listed, each name after what it reads and once.

-- the level of a name among the live names: 0 when it reads none of them, else one more than the
-- highest level of those it reads; in as many rounds as there are nodes, which an acyclic
-- dataflow does not exhaust
level (ns : List Node) (live : List String) (k : Nat) (x : String) : Nat :=
  if k == 0 then 0 else highest ns live (k - 1) (keep live (readsOf ns x))
highest (ns : List Node) (live : List String) (k : Nat) (xs : List String) : Nat :=
  fold String Nat (fn (h r : Nat) { if h > r then h else r }) 0 (fn (x : String) { indicator true + level ns live k x }) xs
-- the levels along a schedule never fall
-- kept as a recursion (bite 13b): the previous level is threaded along the schedule
byLevels (ns : List Node) (live : List String) (prev : Nat) (s : Schedule) : Bool :=
  match s { nil -> true ; cons x rest -> {
    l := level ns live (size ns) x
    prev <= l and byLevels ns live l rest } }
-- the order of first demand: a name is placed after the names it reads, visited in the order its
-- node lists them, and once; bounded by the number of nodes
demandFrom (ns : List Node) (x : String) (done : List String) (k : Nat) : List String :=
  if member List String x done or k == 0 then done else demandAll ns (readsOf ns x) done (k - 1) <> [x]
demandAll (ns : List Node) (xs : List String) (done : List String) (k : Nat) : List String :=
  foldLeft String (List String) (fn (dn : List String) (x : String) { demandFrom ns x dn k }) done xs
firstDemand (A : U) (eq : A -> A -> Bool) (d : Dataflow A eq) (entry : String) : Schedule :=
  demandFrom d.nodes entry nil (1 + size d.nodes)

-- A plan: the strategy that chose it, the entry, the live subgraph and a schedule of it
-- (D-2026-10-13-g: the plan is a value; L5.6: its hash enters the identity of a result).
Plan (A : U) = { strategy : Strategy, entry : String, live : List String, schedule : Schedule }

-- The backward pass from a demand and a program to the dataflow of its cone (8.S4: a demand's plan
-- is the dataflow of its cone; 8.S11: a function from a demand and a program to a plan, not
-- written): a hole. The values of the dataflow are terms, the kernel's reduction its `step`
-- (term.lth §5). The equality of the terms is the plan's parameter, as it is `Planning`'s (4.R8).
-- [proposed, B20 of summary-BCD.md] It takes the demand, whose holes filled and type demanded
-- change the cone (8.S11, 8.S8); from the program alone the plan of a demand with `--set` or a
-- decoration was the plan of the unset, undecorated program.
dataflowOf : (eq : Term -> Term -> Bool) -> Demand -> Program -> Dataflow Term eq
-- and the plan of a demand on a program, by the strategy the demand asks (D-2026-10-16-d; forward on
-- demand by default, demand_model.lut's `theDemand`). run.py computes a demand for forward on
-- demand by call by need, its specimen, and records the strategy that ran in its plan; the two
-- agree by `TheDefaultsAgree` (8.S4).
planOf (eq : Term -> Term -> Bool) (p : Planning Term eq) (d : Demand) (prog : Program) : Plan Term :=
  p.plan d.strategy (dataflowOf eq d prog) d.entry

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- §4 The key of a result

-- Of the demand, the key holds only what the cone reads (8.S8): the type demanded, always read,
-- and the values given to holes that are live; a parameter the cone does not read leaves the key
-- as it was.
DemandKey = { decoration : Maybe Decoration, values : List (String * Value) }
keepRead (live : List String) (vs : List (String * Value)) : List (String * Value) :=
  filter List (String * Value) (fn (nv : String * Value) { match nv { (n, v) -> member List String n live } }) vs
demandKey (d : Demand) (live : List String) : DemandKey := { decoration := d.decoration, values := keepRead live d.sets }
withSet (d : Demand) (n : String) (v : Value) : Demand :=
  { entry := d.entry, decoration := d.decoration, accepts := d.accepts, assumes := d.assumes, delta := d.delta,
    fuel := d.fuel, timeLimit := d.timeLimit, sets := cons (n, v) d.sets, checked := d.checked, pinned := d.pinned,
    strategy := d.strategy, fresh := d.fresh, axioms := d.axioms, roots := d.roots, combine := d.combine, bound := d.bound }

-- The identity of a result (8.S8, L5.6, D-2026-10-13-g): the demand's key, the hash of the cone
-- (the code, the hosts behind its externs and the interpreter, certification.lth §4), the mode,
-- the seed, the hash of the plan, and the hashes of the certificates of the live cone. A hit
-- serves a demand only with an equal key (8.S9); the store that holds it is `x.results.json`
-- (8.S10, `ResultsDetermined` below). [proposed] The mode is a string: 8.S1 names `m` and the spec
-- does not define it; today the only mode is `--checked`, printed. The strategy is not a field:
-- it is the plan's, so the plan's hash carries it (the strategy that ran, not the one asked, which
-- the record keeps; the two give one result by `TheDefaultsAgree`). Neither `fresh` nor the limits
-- are in the key: `fresh` decides whether the store is read, and a limit only cuts a run
-- (D-2026-10-15-g).
MemoKey = { demand : DemandKey, cone : Hash, mode : String, seed : Seed, plan : Hash, certificates : List Hash }
withDemand (k : MemoKey) (dk : DemandKey) : MemoKey :=
  { demand := dk, cone := k.cone, mode := k.mode, seed := k.seed, plan := k.plan, certificates := k.certificates }
withCone (k : MemoKey) (h : Hash) : MemoKey :=
  { demand := k.demand, cone := h, mode := k.mode, seed := k.seed, plan := k.plan, certificates := k.certificates }
withMode (k : MemoKey) (m : String) : MemoKey :=
  { demand := k.demand, cone := k.cone, mode := m, seed := k.seed, plan := k.plan, certificates := k.certificates }
withSeed (k : MemoKey) (s : Seed) : MemoKey :=
  { demand := k.demand, cone := k.cone, mode := k.mode, seed := s, plan := k.plan, certificates := k.certificates }
withPlan (k : MemoKey) (h : Hash) : MemoKey :=
  { demand := k.demand, cone := k.cone, mode := k.mode, seed := k.seed, plan := h, certificates := k.certificates }
withCertificates (k : MemoKey) (hs : List Hash) : MemoKey :=
  { demand := k.demand, cone := k.cone, mode := k.mode, seed := k.seed, plan := k.plan, certificates := hs }

-- The hash of a key and of a plan are the host's, as the hash of a cone is (certification.lth
-- §4). [restated 2026-10-23, audit 3.4, record L5.6, 8.S8, 8.S9] The key is the identity of a
-- result; its hash is a digest, a function of the key (8.S2: equal demands give equal keys, which
-- a function gives), kept as a short name for it. A digest with a finite codomain cannot be
-- injective on an unbounded space of keys, so no law here says it is. A lookup compares the full
-- key (`serves`, run.py's `served_by`, which compares the key and its hash both) and the hash
-- only finds the candidates. What a finite test can show is that, over the cases it lists, two
-- keys that differ in one input have different digests: collision evidence on those cases. A
-- sample that finds a collision refutes the model; one that finds none says nothing beyond the
-- sample. The laws of the lookup say that it holds on a collision (`LookupComparesTheFullKey`)
-- and that a cone with an action is never served from the memo (`ActionConeIsNeverServed`, L4.7:
-- a definition's result depends only on its inputs, an action's does not). `serves` takes whether
-- the cone is pure (no action in it), the key stored and the key asked.
Keying (A : U) : { key : MemoKey -> Hash, planHash : Plan A -> Hash, runKey : RunRecord -> Seed -> Plan A -> List Hash -> Hash,
  serves : Bool -> MemoKey -> MemoKey -> Bool }

-- The key of a run from what it records (D-2026-10-15-h: the record says how to reproduce a run,
-- the key when two results are the same result): of its record (demand.lth's `Record`), the type
-- demanded and the values of the holes the plan's live cone reads, the cone it ran and whether it
-- ran checked; its seed; the hash of its plan; the hashes of the certificates that served its
-- cone. The fuel, the time and the lock are in the record and not in the key (D-2026-10-15-g).
-- [proposed] The plan's hash in the key is that of the plan as chosen, before its schedule: call by
-- need writes the schedule as it runs (8.S4), and a key read before evaluating cannot hold it; the
-- schedule follows from the cone and the values the rest of the key holds (`ByNeedIsFirstDemand`),
-- so leaving it out of the key distinguishes no two results the rest does not.
chosen (A : U) (p : Plan A) : Plan A := { strategy := p.strategy, entry := p.entry, live := p.live, schedule := nil }
modeOf (r : RunRecord) : String := if r.checked then "checked" else "plain"
keyOf (A : U) (h : Keying A) (r : RunRecord) (s : Seed) (p : Plan A) (cs : List Hash) : MemoKey :=
  { demand := { decoration := r.decoration, values := keepRead p.live r.parameters }, cone := r.cone,
    mode := modeOf r, seed := s, plan := h.planHash (chosen A p), certificates := cs }
-- over the cases listed, a key that differs in one input has another digest (collision evidence, not
-- injectivity: the comment above)
DigestSeparatesTheDemand (A : U) (h : Keying A) (k : MemoKey) (dk : DemandKey) : Bool := dk == k.demand or not (h.key (withDemand k dk) == h.key k)
DigestSeparatesTheCone (A : U) (h : Keying A) (k : MemoKey) (c : Hash) : Bool := c == k.cone or not (h.key (withCone k c) == h.key k)
DigestSeparatesTheMode (A : U) (h : Keying A) (k : MemoKey) (m : String) : Bool := m == k.mode or not (h.key (withMode k m) == h.key k)
DigestSeparatesTheSeed (A : U) (h : Keying A) (k : MemoKey) (s : Seed) : Bool := s == k.seed or not (h.key (withSeed k s) == h.key k)
DigestSeparatesThePlan (A : U) (h : Keying A) (k : MemoKey) (p : Hash) : Bool := p == k.plan or not (h.key (withPlan k p) == h.key k)
DigestSeparatesTheCertificates (A : U) (h : Keying A) (k : MemoKey) (hs : List Hash) : Bool :=
  hs == k.certificates or not (h.key (withCertificates k hs) == h.key k)
PlanDigestSeparatesTheSchedule (A : U) (h : Keying A) (p : Plan A) (s : Schedule) : Bool :=
  s == p.schedule or not (h.planHash { strategy := p.strategy, entry := p.entry, live := p.live, schedule := s } == h.planHash p)
-- the lookup serves a pure cone's result only on an equal key, whatever the digests say
LookupComparesTheFullKey (A : U) (h : Keying A) (stored asked : MemoKey) : Bool := h.serves true stored asked == (stored == asked)
-- a cone with an action is never served from the memo (L4.7), whatever the keys
ActionConeIsNeverServed (A : U) (h : Keying A) (stored asked : MemoKey) : Bool := not (h.serves false stored asked)
-- D-2026-10-15-h: the key a run computes is the hash of `keyOf` of what it records, so a model
-- that hashed the fuel, the time or the lock, or left out a field of the key, fails it
KeyIsOfTheRecord (A : U) (h : Keying A) (r : RunRecord) (s : Seed) (p : Plan A) (cs : List Hash) : Bool :=
  h.runKey r s p cs == h.key (keyOf A h r s p cs)
Keying (A : U) := DigestSeparatesTheDemand A & DigestSeparatesTheCone A & DigestSeparatesTheMode A & DigestSeparatesTheSeed A & DigestSeparatesThePlan A
  & DigestSeparatesTheCertificates A & PlanDigestSeparatesTheSchedule A & LookupComparesTheFullKey A
  & ActionConeIsNeverServed A & KeyIsOfTheRecord A

-- The store of results (8.S3, 8.S10, D-2026-10-15-d): `x.results.json` beside the program, each
-- result printed under the hash of its key; demand.lth's `determined` speaks of the key
-- (D-2026-10-15-h): one key, one result. A run that finds its key's entries disagreeing is not
-- served and keeps its own beside them, the store then breaking this (as an exact replay of a
-- certificate that disagrees does, D-2026-10-15-f), until the discrepancy is resolved.
eqHash (a b : Hash) : Bool := a == b
ResultsDetermined (rs : List (Stored Hash)) : Bool := determined Hash eqHash rs
-- [core bite 13b] gathered so that this file claims it (4.S14); a model of the results store tests it
ResultsStore := ResultsDetermined

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- §5 The theory

-- A model of planning gives, for a strategy, a dataflow and an entry, a plan.
Planning (A : U) (eq : A -> A -> Bool) : { plan : Strategy -> Dataflow A eq -> String -> Plan A }

-- §3. 8.S4, L5.13: a plan is of the strategy and entry asked, and its live set is what the entry
-- reaches, no more and no less
PlanIsTheLiveCone (A : U) (eq : A -> A -> Bool) (p : Planning A eq) (st : Strategy) (d : Dataflow A eq) (e : String) : Bool :=
  (p.plan st d e).strategy == st and (p.plan st d e).entry == e and sameMembers (p.plan st d e).live (reaches A eq d e)
-- 8.S3, L5.2: its schedule linearizes the live cone, each name once, none before what it reads
PlanLinearizes (A : U) (eq : A -> A -> Bool) (p : Planning A eq) (st : Strategy) (d : Dataflow A eq) (e : String) : Bool :=
  LinearizesOn A eq d (p.plan st d e).live (p.plan st d e).schedule
-- 8.S4, 8.S5: two strategies give one result on the live cone (an instance of `Confluent`)
StrategiesAgree (A : U) (eq : A -> A -> Bool) (p : Planning A eq) (s1 s2 : Strategy) (d : Dataflow A eq) (e : String) : Bool :=
  EquivalentOn A eq d (reaches A eq d e) (p.plan s1 d e).schedule (p.plan s2 d e).schedule
-- 8.S4: the two strategies named, call by need (run.py today) and forward on demand (8.S3's
-- default), compute the same live subgraph and give every name of it one value
TheDefaultsAgree (A : U) (eq : A -> A -> Bool) (p : Planning A eq) (d : Dataflow A eq) (e : String) : Bool :=
  sameMembers (p.plan CallByNeed d e).live (p.plan ForwardOnDemand d e).live
    and EquivalentOn A eq d (reaches A eq d e) (p.plan CallByNeed d e).schedule (p.plan ForwardOnDemand d e).schedule
-- 8.S11, L5.11: the dataflow of a plan is confluent: the plan's schedule and any linearization
-- of its live cone, built from drawn choices, give every live name one value [proposed, B11 of
-- summary-BCD.md: over two schedules drawn whole the premise almost never held, and the law did
-- not mention the plan]
PlanIsConfluent (A : U) (eq : A -> A -> Bool) (p : Planning A eq) (st : Strategy) (d : Dataflow A eq) (e : String) (cs : List Nat) : Bool :=
  Confluent A eq d (reaches A eq d e) (p.plan st d e).schedule (linearization A eq d (reaches A eq d e) cs)
-- §3. L2.7, 8.S3, 8.S4: the role of each strategy, an order: forward on demand by levels, call
-- by need in the order of first demand. [proposed] Without these a planner that gives one schedule
-- for both passes every law above (summary-BCD.md, B9).
ForwardIsByLevels (A : U) (eq : A -> A -> Bool) (p : Planning A eq) (d : Dataflow A eq) (e : String) : Bool :=
  byLevels d.nodes (p.plan ForwardOnDemand d e).live 0 (p.plan ForwardOnDemand d e).schedule
ByNeedIsFirstDemand (A : U) (eq : A -> A -> Bool) (p : Planning A eq) (d : Dataflow A eq) (e : String) : Bool :=
  (p.plan CallByNeed d e).schedule == firstDemand A eq d e
-- [2026-10-23, audit 3.3, L4.7, 8.S5, 8.S11] Determinacy of a pure cone under any strategy, stated as
-- a law conditional on L4.7: when no step of the dataflow reads outside what its node lists (no
-- action in the cone, `StepIsLocal` on the environments listed), any two strategies give every name
-- of the live cone one value. It claims nothing of a cone with an action or of host nondeterminism
-- (L5.7: scheduling can change numerical bits); such a cone is never served from the memo
-- (`ActionConeIsNeverServed`).
PureConeIsDeterminate (A : U) (eq : A -> A -> Bool) (p : Planning A eq) (d : Dataflow A eq) (e : String) (envs : List (String -> A))
    (s1 s2 : Strategy) : Bool :=
  not (all List String (fn (n : String) { all List (String -> A) (fn (env : String -> A) { StepIsLocal A eq d n env }) envs }) (names d.nodes))
    or EquivalentOn A eq d (reaches A eq d e) (p.plan s1 d e).schedule (p.plan s2 d e).schedule
-- §4. 8.S8: a value given to a hole the cone does not read leaves the demand's key as it was. The
-- key reads the plan's live set (`demandKey`), so the planner enters through it: the hole is one
-- the entry does not reach in the dataflow, and a planner whose live set is wider than the cone
-- (the whole graph, plan_controls.test.lut's `wholeGraph`) puts the hole into the key and fails
-- this; one whose live set is the cone leaves the key as it was. [restated 2026-10-17 by Claude
-- Fable 5.1 on record/IA/regions-2026-10-17/prompt-theory.md, item 4; L9.14] Before, the hole
-- was tested against the plan's own live set, which `demandKey` reads, so the law held of every
-- planner by the definition (B13 of summary-BCD.md) and no control could fail it; tested against
-- what the entry reaches it is a law of `Planning`, claimed below. The second statement of 8.S8,
-- that the type demanded is always in the key (`KeyReadsTheType`, until this draft), is
-- `demandKey`'s definition (`decoration := d.decoration`) and no planner enters it: the claim a
-- model can fail is `Keying`'s `DigestSeparatesTheDemand` on two keys that differ in the decoration (a
-- value and its derivative have two keys), which waits for a model of `Keying` (8.S10, the result
-- store). Removed, not restated.
KeyReadsOnlyTheCone (A : U) (eq : A -> A -> Bool) (p : Planning A eq) (st : Strategy) (d : Dataflow A eq) (dm : Demand) (n : String) (v : Value) : Bool :=
  member List String n (reaches A eq d dm.entry)
    or demandKey (withSet dm n v) (p.plan st d dm.entry).live == demandKey dm (p.plan st d dm.entry).live

Planning (A : U) (eq : A -> A -> Bool) := PlanIsTheLiveCone A eq & PlanLinearizes A eq & StrategiesAgree A eq
  & TheDefaultsAgree A eq & ForwardIsByLevels A eq & ByNeedIsFirstDemand A eq & PlanIsConfluent A eq
  & KeyReadsOnlyTheCone A eq & PureConeIsDeterminate A eq
